<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       ARCHONS: NEVER RAID ON THEIR OWN INITIATIVE

       VRE_Archons ships with earliestRaidDays = 45, meaning an Archotech
       tier faction can raid a 45-day-old colony. In a playthrough that
       spends its first several years in the neolithic era, that is fatal.

       We push it out of reach rather than deleting the faction, because:
         - the faction must exist at worldgen for our quest chain to have
           something to summon;
         - hidden = true already keeps them off the faction list;
         - they generate no settlements, so they cost nothing to leave in.

       DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED: permanentEnemy stays true. "Joining" the
       archons in this playthrough means acquiring the VRE_Transcendent
       gene, not forming an alliance. Leaving permanentEnemy true keeps
       them out of trade, peace talks, and every other diplomatic system,
       which is the intended "man behind the curtain" behaviour.

       Ignorance Is Bliss (useActualTechLevel = true) should already keep
       Archotech factions out of the hostile pool until the player reaches
       that tier. This patch is a second, independent line of defence.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Races Expanded - Archon</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="VRE_Archons"]/earliestRaidDays</xpath>
      <value>
        <earliestRaidDays>999999</earliestRaidDays>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
